{"code": "es", "name": "Spanish", "native": "Español", "phase": 1, "medium": "en", "file_level": "A1", "pronunciation": {"title": "Say it right from day one", "rules": [{"rule": "Vowels never change", "explain": "a=AH, e=EH, i=EE, o=OH, u=OO. Always. So CASA is KAH-sah.", "examples": [{"t": "casa", "r": "KAH-sah", "en": "house"}, {"t": "mesa", "r": "MEH-sah", "en": "table"}]}, {"rule": "H is silent, J sounds like H", "explain": "HOLA is OH-lah (no H sound). J in JUEVES sounds like English H: HWEH-vehs.", "examples": [{"t": "hola", "r": "OH-lah", "en": "hello"}, {"t": "jueves", "r": "HWEH-vehs", "en": "Thursday"}]}, {"rule": "Ñ = NY, LL/Y = Y", "explain": "Ñ is like NY in canyon: NIÑO = NEEN-yoh. LL and Y sound like Y in yes.", "examples": [{"t": "niño", "r": "NEEN-yoh", "en": "boy"}, {"t": "calle", "r": "KAH-yeh", "en": "street"}]}, {"rule": "R rolls a little", "explain": "Tap your tongue once for R. PERRO (dog) rolls longer than PERO (but).", "examples": [{"t": "pero", "r": "PEH-roh", "en": "but"}, {"t": "perro", "r": "PEH-rroh", "en": "dog"}]}, {"rule": "Stress the second-last syllable", "explain": "Most words stress the middle: HOLA = OH-lah, GRACIAS = GRAH-syahs. An accent mark (á) forces stress there.", "examples": [{"t": "gracias", "r": "GRAH-syahs", "en": "thanks"}, {"t": "café", "r": "kah-FEH", "en": "coffee"}]}]}, "alphabet": {"title": "The Spanish alphabet: 27 letters", "explain": "Spanish uses the same letters as English plus Ñ. Letter names matter for spelling your name aloud. Read each name, then say the example word.", "letters": [{"t": "a", "r": "ah", "tip": "as in father: CASA"}, {"t": "b", "r": "beh", "tip": "soft, lips barely touch: BOCA"}, {"t": "c", "r": "seh", "tip": "CA=K, CE/CI=S: CENA"}, {"t": "d", "r": "deh", "tip": "soft, like TH in this: DÍA"}, {"t": "e", "r": "eh", "tip": "as in bet: MESA"}, {"t": "f", "r": "EH-feh", "tip": "same as English: FOTO"}, {"t": "g", "r": "heh", "tip": "GA=hard G, GE/J=silent H: GENTE"}, {"t": "h", "r": "AH-cheh", "tip": "always silent: HOLA = OH-lah"}, {"t": "i", "r": "ee", "tip": "as in machine: SÍ"}, {"t": "j", "r": "HOH-tah", "tip": "strong H sound: JUEVES"}, {"t": "k", "r": "kah", "tip": "rare, foreign words: KILO"}, {"t": "l", "r": "EH-leh", "tip": "same as English: LIBRO"}, {"t": "m", "r": "EH-meh", "tip": "same as English: MANO"}, {"t": "n", "r": "EH-neh", "tip": "same as English: NOCHE"}, {"t": "ñ", "r": "EH-nyeh", "tip": "NY as in canyon: NIÑO"}, {"t": "o", "r": "oh", "tip": "short, as in hot: OJO"}, {"t": "p", "r": "peh", "tip": "same, less puff: PAN"}, {"t": "q", "r": "koo", "tip": "always QU = K: QUESO"}, {"t": "r", "r": "EH-reh", "tip": "single tap: PERO"}, {"t": "s", "r": "EH-seh", "tip": "always S, never Z: SÍ"}, {"t": "t", "r": "teh", "tip": "same as English: TÍO"}, {"t": "u", "r": "oo", "tip": "as in moon: LUNA"}, {"t": "v", "r": "oo-beh", "tip": "sounds like soft B: VINO"}, {"t": "w", "r": "oo-beh-DOH-bleh", "tip": "rare, foreign words: WEB"}, {"t": "x", "r": "EH-kees", "tip": "KS sound: TAXI"}, {"t": "y", "r": "ee-gree-EH-gah", "tip": "Y in yes, or EE alone: YO"}, {"t": "z", "r": "SEH-tah", "tip": "S sound (Latin America): ZAPATO"}]}, "counting": {"title": "Counting 0 to 100", "explain": "Learn 0–15 by heart. 16–19 = DIEZ + number stuck together (dieciséis). 20s = VEINTI + number (veintidós). 30+ = tens + Y + ones (treinta y uno). 100 = CIEN (cien alone, ciento + more).", "numbers": [{"t": "cero", "r": "SEH-roh", "en": "0"}, {"t": "uno", "r": "OO-noh", "en": "1"}, {"t": "dos", "r": "dohs", "en": "2"}, {"t": "tres", "r": "trehs", "en": "3"}, {"t": "cuatro", "r": "KWAH-troh", "en": "4"}, {"t": "cinco", "r": "SEEN-koh", "en": "5"}, {"t": "seis", "r": "seh-ees", "en": "6"}, {"t": "siete", "r": "SYEH-teh", "en": "7"}, {"t": "ocho", "r": "OH-choh", "en": "8"}, {"t": "nueve", "r": "NWEH-veh", "en": "9"}, {"t": "diez", "r": "dyehs", "en": "10"}, {"t": "once", "r": "OHN-seh", "en": "11"}, {"t": "doce", "r": "DOH-seh", "en": "12"}, {"t": "trece", "r": "TREH-seh", "en": "13"}, {"t": "catorce", "r": "kah-TOHR-seh", "en": "14"}, {"t": "quince", "r": "KEEN-seh", "en": "15"}, {"t": "dieciséis", "r": "dyeh-see-SEH-ees", "en": "16"}, {"t": "diecisiete", "r": "dyeh-see-SYEH-teh", "en": "17"}, {"t": "dieciocho", "r": "dyeh-see-OH-choh", "en": "18"}, {"t": "diecinueve", "r": "dyeh-see-NWEH-veh", "en": "19"}, {"t": "veinte", "r": "BEH-een-teh", "en": "20"}, {"t": "treinta", "r": "TREH-een-tah", "en": "30"}, {"t": "cuarenta", "r": "kwah-REHN-tah", "en": "40"}, {"t": "cincuenta", "r": "seen-KWEHN-tah", "en": "50"}, {"t": "sesenta", "r": "seh-SEHN-tah", "en": "60"}, {"t": "setenta", "r": "seh-TEHN-tah", "en": "70"}, {"t": "ochenta", "r": "oh-CHEHN-tah", "en": "80"}, {"t": "noventa", "r": "noh-BEHN-tah", "en": "90"}, {"t": "cien", "r": "syehn", "en": "100"}], "rules": ["16–29 are glued together: dieciséis (16), veintidós (22).", "30–99 use Y: treinta y uno (31), cuarenta y dos (42).", "CIEN = exactly 100; CIENTO + more: ciento uno (101)."]}, "level": {"title": "Beginner: first words, family, food", "goals": ["Greet people and introduce yourself", "Count, tell age, talk about family", "Order food and use basic present-tense verbs"], "units": [{"id": "A1-U1", "title": "First words", "lessons": [{"id": "A1-U1-L1", "title": "Hello! Greetings and politeness", "learn": "Start with the magic words. Say HOLA to anyone, anytime. Spanish greets the day in parts: morning (buenos días), afternoon/evening (buenas tardes), night (buenas noches). POR FAVOR (please) and GRACIAS (thanks) open every door.", "vocab": [{"t": "hola", "r": "OH-lah", "en": "hello", "pos": "greeting"}, {"t": "buenos días", "r": "BWEH-nohs DEE-ahs", "en": "good morning", "pos": "greeting"}, {"t": "buenas tardes", "r": "BWEH-nahs TAHR-dehs", "en": "good afternoon/evening", "pos": "greeting"}, {"t": "buenas noches", "r": "BWEH-nahs NOH-chehs", "en": "good night", "pos": "greeting"}, {"t": "adiós", "r": "ah-DYOHS", "en": "goodbye", "pos": "greeting"}, {"t": "por favor", "r": "pohr fah-VOHR", "en": "please", "pos": "adverb"}, {"t": "gracias", "r": "GRAH-syahs", "en": "thanks", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "perdón", "r": "pehr-DOHN", "en": "sorry / excuse me", "pos": "noun"}], "grammar": {"title": "Every noun is EL or LA", "explain": "Spanish nouns are masculine (EL) or feminine (LA). Words ending in -o are usually EL; words ending in -a are usually LA. Learn each noun WITH its el/la — never alone.", "pattern": "el + masculine noun · la + feminine noun", "examples": [{"t": "el libro", "r": "ehl LEE-broh", "en": "the book"}, {"t": "la casa", "r": "lah KAH-sah", "en": "the house"}, {"t": "el agua", "r": "ehl AH-gwah", "en": "the water (looks odd, still feminine!)"}], "mistakes": ["Saying LA libro — libro is masculine: EL libro.", "Forgetting el/la and saying just Casa — say LA casa."]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "Ana", "t": "¡Hola! Buenos días.", "r": "OH-lah! BWEH-nohs DEE-ahs.", "en": "Hello! Good morning."}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "¡Hola! ¿Cómo estás?", "r": "OH-lah! KOH-moh ehs-TAHS?", "en": "Hello! How are you?"}, {"sp": "Ana", "t": "Muy bien, gracias. ¿Y tú?", "r": "mwee byehn, GRAH-syahs. ee too?", "en": "Very well, thanks. And you?"}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "Bien, gracias. ¡Adiós!", "r": "byehn, GRAH-syahs. ah-DYOHS!", "en": "Fine, thanks. Goodbye!"}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: hello", "answer": "hola"}, {"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: thank you", "answer": "gracias"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "___ días (good morning)", "answer": "buenos"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "Which means 'please'?", "options": ["gracias", "por favor", "hola", "adiós"], "answer": "por favor"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: Buenos días, gracias.", "answer": "Buenos días, gracias."}], "quiz": [{"q": "What does HOLA mean?", "options": ["goodbye", "hello", "please", "sorry"], "answer": 1, "why": "Hola is the universal hello."}, {"q": "How do you say 'thanks'?", "options": ["perdón", "hola", "gracias", "adiós"], "answer": 2, "why": "Gracias = thanks."}, {"q": "BUENAS NOCHES is used…", "options": ["in the morning", "at night", "at lunch", "never"], "answer": 1, "why": "Noches = nights."}, {"q": "EL LIBRO means…", "options": ["the house", "the book", "the water", "the door"], "answer": 1, "why": "Libro (masculine) = book."}, {"q": "Which is feminine?", "options": ["el libro", "la casa", "el agua", "el día"], "answer": 1, "why": "La marks feminine nouns. (El agua is an exception.)"}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Greetings worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Match the Spanish greeting to the time of day.", "items": ["buenos días", "buenas tardes", "buenas noches"], "key": ["morning", "afternoon/evening", "night"]}, {"instruction": "Fill in: el or la.", "items": ["___ casa", "___ libro", "___ mesa (table)"], "key": ["la", "el", "la"]}, {"instruction": "Write the magic words in Spanish.", "items": ["please", "thanks", "sorry"], "key": ["por favor", "gracias", "perdón"]}]}}, {"id": "A1-U1-L2", "title": "Numbers and introductions", "learn": "Numbers 1–10 unlock prices, ages, and phone numbers. To introduce yourself use SER (to be): SOY = I am. Soy Ana = I am Ana. To ask a name: ¿CÓMO TE LLAMAS? (What are you called?).", "vocab": [{"t": "uno", "r": "OO-noh", "en": "one", "pos": "number"}, {"t": "dos", "r": "dohs", "en": "two", "pos": "number"}, {"t": "tres", "r": "trehs", "en": "three", "pos": "number"}, {"t": "cuatro", "r": "KWAH-troh", "en": "four", "pos": "number"}, {"t": "cinco", "r": "SEEN-koh", "en": "five", "pos": "number"}, {"t": "seis", "r": "seh-ees", "en": "six", "pos": "number"}, {"t": "siete", "r": "SYEH-teh", "en": "seven", "pos": "number"}, {"t": "ocho", "r": "OH-choh", "en": "eight", "pos": "number"}, {"t": "nueve", "r": "NWEH-veh", "en": "nine", "pos": "number"}, {"t": "diez", "r": "dyehs", "en": "ten", "pos": "number"}], "grammar": {"title": "SER: soy, eres, es (I am, you are, he/she is)", "explain": "SER describes who you are: name, origin, job. SOY = I am, ERES = you are, ES = he/she is. Drop the pronoun: SOY Ana is enough — no YO needed.", "pattern": "soy + name · eres + … · es + …", "examples": [{"t": "Soy Ana.", "r": "soy AH-nah.", "en": "I am Ana."}, {"t": "¿Eres Pedro?", "r": "EH-rehs PEH-droh?", "en": "Are you Pedro?"}, {"t": "Es español.", "r": "ehs ehs-pahn-YOHL.", "en": "He/She is Spanish."}], "mistakes": ["Saying YO SOY Ana every time — SOY Ana is natural.", "Using ES for yourself — I am is SOY, never ES."]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "Ana", "t": "Hola, soy Ana. ¿Cómo te llamas?", "r": "OH-lah, soy AH-nah. KOH-moh teh YAH-mahs?", "en": "Hello, I am Ana. What is your name?"}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "Soy Ben. ¿De dónde eres?", "r": "soy behn. deh DOHN-deh EH-rehs?", "en": "I am Ben. Where are you from?"}, {"sp": "Ana", "t": "Soy de México.", "r": "soy deh MEH-hee-koh.", "en": "I am from Mexico."}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "¡Mucho gusto!", "r": "MOO-choh GOOS-toh!", "en": "Nice to meet you!"}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: I am Ana", "answer": "Soy Ana"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "___ eres? (who are you?) — no, 'are you Pedro?': ¿___ Pedro?", "answer": "Eres"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'I am' in Spanish is…", "options": ["es", "eres", "soy", "son"], "answer": "soy"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: Ana / soy", "answer": "soy Ana"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: Soy Ben. ¿Cómo te llamas?", "answer": "Soy Ben. ¿Cómo te llamas?"}], "quiz": [{"q": "SOY means…", "options": ["you are", "I am", "he is", "we are"], "answer": 1, "why": "Soy = I am."}, {"q": "How do you ask someone's name?", "options": ["¿Cómo estás?", "¿Cómo te llamas?", "¿De dónde eres?", "¿Cuántos años?"], "answer": 1, "why": "¿Cómo te llamas? = What are you called?"}, {"q": "CINCO is number…", "options": ["3", "4", "5", "6"], "answer": 2, "why": "uno dos tres cuatro CINCO."}, {"q": "'I am from Mexico' is…", "options": ["Soy México", "Soy de México", "Es de México", "Eres México"], "answer": 1, "why": "Soy de + place = I am from."}, {"q": "MUCHO GUSTO means…", "options": ["goodbye", "nice to meet you", "see you", "good luck"], "answer": 1, "why": "Say it when you first meet someone."}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Numbers and names worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Write the numbers in Spanish.", "items": ["2", "5", "10"], "key": ["dos", "cinco", "diez"]}, {"instruction": "Complete with soy, eres, or es.", "items": ["___ Ana (I am)", "¿___ Pedro? (are you)", "___ español (he is)"], "key": ["Soy", "Eres", "Es"]}, {"instruction": "Introduce yourself in two lines.", "items": ["Say your name", "Say where you are from"], "key": ["Soy …", "Soy de …"]}]}}]}, {"id": "A1-U2", "title": "Daily life", "lessons": [{"id": "A1-U2-L1", "title": "Family and TENER (age)", "learn": "Meet the family: MADRE (mother), PADRE (father), HERMANO/A (brother/sister). Age uses TENER (to have), not 'to be': TENGO 10 AÑOS = I have 10 years = I am 10 years old.", "vocab": [{"t": "la madre", "r": "lah MAH-dreh", "en": "mother", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "el padre", "r": "ehl PAH-dreh", "en": "father", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "el hermano", "r": "ehl ehr-MAH-noh", "en": "brother", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "la hermana", "r": "lah ehr-MAH-nah", "en": "sister", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "el hijo", "r": "ehl EE-hoh", "en": "son", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "la hija", "r": "lah EE-hah", "en": "daughter", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "la familia", "r": "lah fah-MEE-lyah", "en": "family", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "el amigo / la amiga", "r": "ehl ah-MEE-goh", "en": "friend (m/f)", "pos": "noun"}], "grammar": {"title": "TENER for age: tengo… años", "explain": "TENGO = I have, TIENES = you have, TIENE = he/she has. For age: TENGO + number + AÑOS. Ask age: ¿CUÁNTOS AÑOS TIENES? (How many years do you have?).", "pattern": "tengo/tienes/tiene + number + años", "examples": [{"t": "Tengo diez años.", "r": "TEHN-goh dyehs AHN-yohs.", "en": "I am 10 years old."}, {"t": "¿Cuántos años tienes?", "r": "KWAHN-tohs AHN-yohs TYEH-nehs?", "en": "How old are you?"}, {"t": "Mi hermana tiene siete años.", "r": "mee ehr-MAH-nah TYEH-neh SYEH-teh AHN-yohs.", "en": "My sister is 7."}], "mistakes": ["Saying SOY diez años — age always uses TENER.", "Saying AÑOS without T: ANOS is a rude word — say AHN-yohs with Ñ!"]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "Ana", "t": "¿Tienes hermanos?", "r": "TYEH-nehs ehr-MAH-nohs?", "en": "Do you have brothers/sisters?"}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "Sí, tengo un hermano y una hermana.", "r": "see, TEHN-goh oon ehr-MAH-noh ee OO-nah ehr-MAH-nah.", "en": "Yes, I have one brother and one sister."}, {"sp": "Ana", "t": "¿Cuántos años tiene tu hermana?", "r": "KWAHN-tohs AHN-yohs TYEH-neh too ehr-MAH-nah?", "en": "How old is your sister?"}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "Tiene siete años.", "r": "TYEH-neh SYEH-teh AHN-yohs.", "en": "She is seven."}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: I am 10 years old", "answer": "Tengo diez años"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "Mi hermano ___ ocho años. (has)", "answer": "tiene"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'How old are you?' is…", "options": ["¿Cómo estás?", "¿Cuántos años tienes?", "¿Cómo te llamas?", "¿De dónde eres?"], "answer": "¿Cuántos años tienes?"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: años / tengo / diez", "answer": "tengo diez años"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: Tengo un hermano.", "answer": "Tengo un hermano."}], "quiz": [{"q": "TENGO DIEZ AÑOS means…", "options": ["I have ten houses", "I am ten years old", "I like ten songs", "I see ten birds"], "answer": 1, "why": "Tener + años = age."}, {"q": "LA HERMANA is…", "options": ["brother", "sister", "mother", "daughter"], "answer": 1, "why": "-a ending: sister."}, {"q": "Which asks about age?", "options": ["¿Cómo estás?", "¿Cuántos años tienes?", "¿Dónde vives?", "¿Qué hora es?"], "answer": 1, "why": "Cuántos años = how many years."}, {"q": "'My sister is 7' is…", "options": ["Mi hermana tiene siete años", "Mi hermana es siete", "Mi hermana siete años", "Tengo hermana siete"], "answer": 0, "why": "Tiene + number + años."}, {"q": "UN HERMANO Y UNA HERMANA means…", "options": ["two brothers", "two sisters", "a brother and a sister", "no siblings"], "answer": 2, "why": "Un = a (m), una = a (f)."}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Family worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Translate to Spanish.", "items": ["mother", "brother", "family"], "key": ["la madre", "el hermano", "la familia"]}, {"instruction": "Write the age sentence.", "items": ["I am 8 (years)", "My brother is 5"], "key": ["Tengo ocho años", "Mi hermano tiene cinco años"]}, {"instruction": "Answer about yourself.", "items": ["¿Tienes hermanos?", "¿Cuántos años tienes?"], "key": ["Sí/No, (tengo…)", "Tengo … años"]}]}}, {"id": "A1-U2-L2", "title": "Food and -AR verbs", "learn": "Food first! AGUA, PAN, LECHE, MANZANA. To order, use QUIERO (I want) or QUISIERA (I would like, politer). Most Spanish verbs end in -AR: HABLAR (to speak) → HABLO (I speak), HABLAS (you speak), HABLA (he/she speaks).", "vocab": [{"t": "el agua", "r": "ehl AH-gwah", "en": "water", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "el pan", "r": "ehl pahn", "en": "bread", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "la leche", "r": "lah LEH-cheh", "en": "milk", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "la manzana", "r": "lah mahn-SAH-nah", "en": "apple", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "el arroz", "r": "ehl ah-RROHS", "en": "rice", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "el pollo", "r": "ehl POH-yoh", "en": "chicken", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "el café", "r": "ehl kah-FEH", "en": "coffee", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "el té", "r": "ehl teh", "en": "tea", "pos": "noun"}], "grammar": {"title": "Present -AR verbs: hablo, hablas, habla", "explain": "Take off -AR, add -O (I), -AS (you), -A (he/she). HABLAR → hablo, hablas, habla. This one pattern speaks hundreds of verbs: COMO (I eat), BEBO? No — BEBER is -ER. For now: -AR only!", "pattern": "verb stem + o/as/a", "examples": [{"t": "Hablo español.", "r": "AH-bloh ehs-pahn-YOHL.", "en": "I speak Spanish."}, {"t": "¿Hablas inglés?", "r": "AH-blahs een-GLEHS?", "en": "Do you speak English?"}, {"t": "Ella canta bien.", "r": "EH-yah KAHN-tah byehn.", "en": "She sings well."}], "mistakes": ["Saying YO HABLAS for 'I speak' — I = HABLO, you = HABLAS.", "Keeping the -AR: HABLO, not HABLARO."]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "Ben", "t": "¡Buenas tardes! Quisiera un café, por favor.", "r": "BWEH-nahs TAHR-dehs! kee-SYEH-rah oon kah-FEH, pohr fah-VOHR.", "en": "Good afternoon! I would like a coffee, please."}, {"sp": "Ana", "t": "¿Grande o pequeño?", "r": "GRAHN-deh oh peh-KEH-nyoh?", "en": "Large or small?"}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "Grande, gracias. ¿Cuánto es?", "r": "GRAHN-deh, GRAH-syahs. KWAHN-toh ehs?", "en": "Large, thanks. How much is it?"}, {"sp": "Ana", "t": "Dos euros.", "r": "dohs eh-OO-rohs.", "en": "Two euros."}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: I speak Spanish", "answer": "Hablo español"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "¿___ inglés? (do YOU speak)", "answer": "Hablas"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'I would like a coffee' starts with…", "options": ["Quiero", "Quisiera", "Tengo", "Soy"], "answer": "Quisiera"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: café / quisiera / un", "answer": "quisiera un café"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: Quisiera un té, por favor.", "answer": "Quisiera un té, por favor."}], "quiz": [{"q": "HABLAS means…", "options": ["I speak", "you speak", "he speaks", "they speak"], "answer": 1, "why": "-AS = you."}, {"q": "EL POLLO is…", "options": ["bread", "rice", "chicken", "apple"], "answer": 2, "why": "Pollo = chicken."}, {"q": "¿CUÁNTO ES? means…", "options": ["Where is it?", "How much is it?", "What time is it?", "Who is it?"], "answer": 1, "why": "Cuánto = how much."}, {"q": "'She sings well' is…", "options": ["Ella canto bien", "Ella canta bien", "Ella cantas bien", "Ella cantar bien"], "answer": 1, "why": "She = -A: canta."}, {"q": "Which is the polite order word?", "options": ["quiero", "quisiera", "tengo", "dame"], "answer": 1, "why": "Quisiera = I would like (softer)."}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Food worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Translate to Spanish.", "items": ["water", "milk", "apple"], "key": ["el agua", "la leche", "la manzana"]}, {"instruction": "Conjugate HABLAR.", "items": ["I speak", "you speak", "she speaks"], "key": ["hablo", "hablas", "habla"]}, {"instruction": "Order politely in a café.", "items": ["a coffee, please", "How much is it?"], "key": ["Quisiera un café, por favor", "¿Cuánto es?"]}]}}]}, {"id": "A1-U3", "title": "Describing words", "lessons": [{"id": "A1-U3-L1", "title": "Colors and adjectives", "learn": "Adjectives match their noun: ROJO (red, masculine) but ROJA casa? No — LA casa ROJA. Ending -O goes with EL, -A goes with LA. Position: AFTER the noun — LA CASA BLANCA (the white house).", "vocab": [{"t": "rojo", "r": "ROH-hoh", "en": "red", "pos": "adjective"}, {"t": "azul", "r": "ah-SOOL", "en": "blue", "pos": "adjective"}, {"t": "verde", "r": "BEHR-deh", "en": "green", "pos": "adjective"}, {"t": "amarillo", "r": "ah-mah-REE-yoh", "en": "yellow", "pos": "adjective"}, {"t": "blanco", "r": "BLAHN-koh", "en": "white", "pos": "adjective"}, {"t": "negro", "r": "NEH-groh", "en": "black", "pos": "adjective"}, {"t": "grande", "r": "GRAHN-deh", "en": "big", "pos": "adjective"}, {"t": "pequeño", "r": "peh-KEH-nyoh", "en": "small", "pos": "adjective"}], "grammar": {"title": "Adjective agreement: -o/-a/-os/-as", "explain": "EL libro ROJO, LA casa ROJA, LOS libros ROJOS, LAS casas ROJAS. Adjectives ending in -E or consonants (verde, azul) change only for plural: verde/verdes.", "pattern": "noun + adjective matching gender and number", "examples": [{"t": "El libro rojo.", "r": "ehl LEE-broh ROH-hoh.", "en": "The red book."}, {"t": "La casa blanca.", "r": "lah KAH-sah BLAHN-kah.", "en": "The white house."}, {"t": "Los zapatos negros.", "r": "lohs sah-PAH-tohs NEH-grohs.", "en": "The black shoes."}], "mistakes": ["Saying LA casa BLANCO — feminine needs BLANCA.", "Putting the adjective first (English order) — Spanish puts it after."]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "Ana", "t": "Me gusta la casa blanca.", "r": "meh GOOS-tah lah KAH-sah BLAHN-kah.", "en": "I like the white house."}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "¿Y el coche rojo?", "r": "ee ehl KOH-cheh ROH-hoh?", "en": "And the red car?"}, {"sp": "Ana", "t": "Es muy bonito.", "r": "ehs mwee boh-NEE-toh.", "en": "It is very pretty."}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "Sí, es grande y rojo.", "r": "see, ehs GRAHN-deh ee ROH-hoh.", "en": "Yes, it is big and red."}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: the red book", "answer": "el libro rojo"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "La casa ___ (white)", "answer": "blanca"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'The black shoes' is…", "options": ["Los zapatos negro", "Los zapatos negros", "Las zapatos negros", "El zapato negros"], "answer": "Los zapatos negros"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: casa / blanca / la", "answer": "la casa blanca"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: Me gusta la casa blanca.", "answer": "Me gusta la casa blanca."}], "quiz": [{"q": "LA CASA BLANCA means…", "options": ["the white house", "the black house", "the big house", "the red house"], "answer": 0, "why": "Casa (f) + blanca (f) = white house."}, {"q": "Why ROJA with CASA?", "options": ["it sounds nice", "adjectives match gender", "all words end in A", "no reason"], "answer": 1, "why": "Feminine noun needs feminine -A."}, {"q": "LOS ZAPATOS NEGROS: why NEGROS?", "options": ["plural masculine", "it is long", "shoes are black", "all adjectives add S only"], "answer": 0, "why": "Masculine plural: -OS."}, {"q": "VERDE (green) in plural is…", "options": ["verdos", "verdes", "verdas", "verde"], "answer": 1, "why": "-E adjectives add only -S."}, {"q": "Adjectives usually go…", "options": ["before the noun", "after the noun", "at sentence start", "nowhere"], "answer": 1, "why": "La casa blanca — after!"}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Colors worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Translate to Spanish.", "items": ["red", "blue", "small"], "key": ["rojo", "azul", "pequeño"]}, {"instruction": "Match the adjective.", "items": ["el libro ___ (red)", "la casa ___ (white)", "los zapatos ___ (black)"], "key": ["rojo", "blanca", "negros"]}, {"instruction": "Describe two things.", "items": ["The white house", "The red car"], "key": ["la casa blanca", "el coche rojo"]}]}}, {"id": "A1-U3-L2", "title": "Days, months, and telling time", "learn": "Days and months are lowercase in Spanish: LUNES, ENERO. Time: ES LA UNA (it is one) but SON LAS DOS (two). Ask: ¿QUÉ HORA ES? Answer: SON LAS + number.", "vocab": [{"t": "lunes", "r": "LOO-nehs", "en": "Monday", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "martes", "r": "MAHR-tehs", "en": "Tuesday", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "miércoles", "r": "MYEHR-koh-lehs", "en": "Wednesday", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "hoy", "r": "oy", "en": "today", "pos": "adverb"}, {"t": "mañana", "r": "mahn-YAH-nah", "en": "tomorrow", "pos": "adverb"}, {"t": "ayer", "r": "ah-YEHR", "en": "yesterday", "pos": "adverb"}, {"t": "la semana", "r": "lah seh-MAH-nah", "en": "week", "pos": "noun"}, {"t": "la hora", "r": "lah OH-rah", "en": "hour / time", "pos": "noun"}], "grammar": {"title": "Telling time: es la… / son las…", "explain": "ES LA UNA (1:00 — singular), SON LAS DOS/TRES… (plural). Half past: Y MEDIA — SON LAS TRES Y MEDIA (3:30). Quarter: Y CUARTO.", "pattern": "es la una · son las + number (+ y media)", "examples": [{"t": "Es la una.", "r": "ehs lah OO-nah.", "en": "It is one o'clock."}, {"t": "Son las tres.", "r": "sohn lahs trehs.", "en": "It is three o'clock."}, {"t": "Son las tres y media.", "r": "sohn lahs trehs ee MEH-dyah.", "en": "It is half past three."}], "mistakes": ["Saying SON LA UNA — one o'clock is ES LA UNA.", "Capitalising days (Lunes) — Spanish days are lowercase."]}, "dialogue": [{"sp": "Ben", "t": "¿Qué hora es?", "r": "keh OH-rah ehs?", "en": "What time is it?"}, {"sp": "Ana", "t": "Son las tres y media.", "r": "sohn lahs trehs ee MEH-dyah.", "en": "It is half past three."}, {"sp": "Ben", "t": "¿Nos vemos mañana?", "r": "nohs BEH-mohs mahn-YAH-nah?", "en": "Shall we meet tomorrow?"}, {"sp": "Ana", "t": "Sí, el martes a las diez.", "r": "see, ehl MAHR-tehs ah lahs dyehs.", "en": "Yes, Tuesday at ten."}], "practice": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: It is three o'clock", "answer": "Son las tres"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "___ la una. (It is)", "answer": "Es"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'Half past three' is…", "options": ["Son las tres", "Son las tres y media", "Es la tres", "Son la tres y media"], "answer": "Son las tres y media"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: hora / qué / es", "answer": "qué hora es"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: Son las tres y media.", "answer": "Son las tres y media."}], "quiz": [{"q": "ES LA UNA is used because…", "options": ["one is lucky", "una is singular", "it is morning", "all times use ES"], "answer": 1, "why": "1:00 is singular: ES LA."}, {"q": "¿QUÉ HORA ES? means…", "options": ["What day is it?", "What time is it?", "Where are you?", "How are you?"], "answer": 1, "why": "Hora = hour/time."}, {"q": "Y MEDIA means…", "options": ["and a quarter", "and a half", "and ten", "o'clock sharp"], "answer": 1, "why": "Media = half."}, {"q": "Spanish days are written…", "options": ["CAPITALISED", "lowercase", "in English", "never"], "answer": 1, "why": "lunes, martes — lowercase."}, {"q": "MAÑANA means…", "options": ["today", "tomorrow", "yesterday", "morning only"], "answer": 1, "why": "Mañana = tomorrow (also morning!)."}], "flashcards": "auto:vocab", "worksheet": {"title": "Time worksheet", "tasks": [{"instruction": "Translate to Spanish.", "items": ["Monday", "today", "week"], "key": ["lunes", "hoy", "la semana"]}, {"instruction": "Write the time.", "items": ["1:00", "3:00", "3:30"], "key": ["Es la una", "Son las tres", "Son las tres y media"]}, {"instruction": "Make a plan.", "items": ["Shall we meet tomorrow?", "Yes, Tuesday at ten"], "key": ["¿Nos vemos mañana?", "Sí, el martes a las diez"]}]}}]}], "test": {"title": "A1 final test", "items": [{"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: good morning", "answer": "buenos días"}, {"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: I am Ben", "answer": "Soy Ben"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "Tengo ___ años (I am 9)", "answer": "nueve"}, {"type": "choose", "q": "'Do you speak English?'", "options": ["¿Hablas inglés?", "¿Hablo inglés?", "¿Habla inglés?", "¿Hablan inglés?"], "answer": "¿Hablas inglés?"}, {"type": "translate_t", "q": "¿Cuánto es?", "answer": "How much is it?"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "___ hermana (my sister)", "answer": "mi"}, {"type": "reorder", "q": "Order: años / tiene / siete", "answer": "tiene siete años"}, {"type": "speak", "q": "Say aloud: Quisiera un café, por favor.", "answer": "Quisiera un café, por favor."}, {"type": "translate_en", "q": "Say: the white house", "answer": "la casa blanca"}, {"type": "fill", "q": "Son las tres y ___ (half)", "answer": "media"}]}}}